  "notes": "West leads the ♥K against 3NT. South has what looks like 9 easy tricks (2 spades, the ♥A, 5 diamonds, and the ♣A). There is a serious problem, however, due to the blockage in the diamond suit.\n\nIf South wins the opening heart lead with the ♥A and cashes the top diamonds, a 3-1 diamond break will doom the contract. The diamond blockage will allow South to cash only 1 of the 2 remaining diamond tricks.\n\nSouth can guard against a 3-1 diamond break by ducking the opening lead in dummy. West must continue hearts to knock out dummy's side entry, but South should duck again.\n\nIf West continues hearts, that trick can be won with the ♥A as South discards one of his blocking diamonds. The diamonds can now be run for 5 tricks even if that suit is 3-1.\n\nIf West switches at trick 3, South can cross in diamonds and discard a diamond on the ♥A. Once again the diamond suit will provide 5 cashable tricks.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♥K against 3NT. South has what looks like 9 easy tricks (2 spades, the ♥A, 5 diamonds, and the ♣A). There is a serious problem, however, due to the blockage in the diamond suit.",
    "If South wins the opening heart lead with the ♥A and cashes the top diamonds, a 3-1 diamond break will doom the contract. The diamond blockage will allow South to cash only 1 of the 2 remaining diamond tricks.",
    "South can guard against a 3-1 diamond break by ducking the opening lead in dummy. West must continue hearts to knock out dummy's side entry, but South should duck again.",
    "If West continues hearts, that trick can be won with the ♥A as South discards one of his blocking diamonds. The diamonds can now be run for 5 tricks even if that suit is 3-1.",
    "If West switches at trick 3, South can cross in diamonds and discard a diamond on the ♥A. Once again the diamond suit will provide 5 cashable tricks."
  ],
